er A equals one half left parenthesis 40 right parenthesis left parenthesis 90 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>40</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>90</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 1,800\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1,800</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle is <math alttext=\"1,800\"><mn>1,800</mn>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A triangle has a base length of <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> centimeters and a height of <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math> centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle?</p>","type":"spr","correct_answer":["1800"]},"createDate":1730147357407,"updateDate":1730147357407}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357407, 1730147357407),
    ($SATQ$f60bb551$SATQ$, $SATQ$2cc3f845-5222-4c22-8764-9d19c7b188fb$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$f8a799fd-779a-424d-a269-42eb9f42bf77$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The area of a rectangle is <math alttext="630"><mn>630</mn>
</math> square inches. The length of the rectangle is <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math> inches. What is the width, in inches, of this rectangle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"26ebfd23-9667-442b-8294-9d42c81e6694","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"37779bb0-1067-4276-8ea9-d8cb825f0f32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2aabcf42-e36a-403d-be4c-c3a87b35c5dd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"315\"><mn>315</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8d85f328-f1ae-47aa-9f75-a14c2afd2c55","content":"<p><math alttext=\"560\"><mn>560</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["26ebfd23-9667-442b-8294-9d42c81e6694"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The area <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>, in square inches, of a rectangle is the product of its length <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math>, in inches, and its width <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math>, in inches; thus, <math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>. It's given that the area of a rectangle is <math alttext="630"><mn>630</mn>
</math> square inches and the length of the rectangle is <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math> inches. Substituting <math alttext="630"><mn>630</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext="630 equals 70 w"><mrow>
	<mn>630</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>70</mn>
		<mi>w</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="9 equals w"><mrow>
	<mn>9</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the width, in inches, of this rectangle is <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the length, not the width, in inches, of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is half the area, in square inches, not the width, in inches, of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the difference between the area, in square inches, and the length, in inches, of the rectangle, not the width, in inches, of the rectangle.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f60bb551","external_id":"2cc3f845-5222-4c22-8764-9d19c7b188fb","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"f8a799fd-779a-424d-a269-42eb9f42bf77","uId":"bccb6500-2979-4783-a862-979a7e0050c4","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The area of a rectangle is <math alttext=\"630\"><mn>630</mn>\n</math> square inches. The length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> inches. What is the width, in inches, of this rectangle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"26ebfd23-9667-442b-8294-9d42c81e6694","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"37779bb0-1067-4276-8ea9-d8cb825f0f32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2aabcf42-e36a-403d-be4c-c3a87b35c5dd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"315\"><mn>315</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8d85f328-f1ae-47aa-9f75-a14c2afd2c55","content":"<p><math alttext=\"560\"><mn>560</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["26ebfd23-9667-442b-8294-9d42c81e6694"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The area <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, in square inches, of a rectangle is the product of its length <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, in inches, and its width <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>, in inches; thus, <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>. It's given that the area of a rectangle is <math alttext=\"630\"><mn>630</mn>\n</math> square inches and the length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> inches. Substituting <math alttext=\"630\"><mn>630</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"630 equals 70 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>630</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>70</mn>\n\t\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"9 equals w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the width, in inches, of this rectangle is <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the length, not the width, in inches, of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is half the area, in square inches, not the width, in inches, of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the difference between the area, in square inches, and the length, in inches, of the rectangle, not the width, in inches, of the rectangle.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959836,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"f60bb551","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1691007959836,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"2cc3f845-5222-4c22-8764-9d19c7b188fb","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"bccb6500-2979-4783-a862-979a7e0050c4","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"keys