-align: left;\">The area of a rectangle is <math alttext=\"630\"><mn>630</mn>\n</math> square inches. The length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> inches. What is the width, in inches, of this rectangle?</p>","externalid":"2cc3f845-5222-4c22-8764-9d19c7b188fb","templateid":"8268c75a-f908-4f28-9c05-506426a07bd2","vaultid":"f8a799fd-779a-424d-a269-42eb9f42bf77","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"26ebfd23-9667-442b-8294-9d42c81e6694","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"37779bb0-1067-4276-8ea9-d8cb825f0f32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2aabcf42-e36a-403d-be4c-c3a87b35c5dd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"315\"><mn>315</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8d85f328-f1ae-47aa-9f75-a14c2afd2c55","content":"<p><math alttext=\"560\"><mn>560</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1691007959836,"updateDate":1691007959836}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959836, 1691007959836),
    ($SATQ$f67255ea$SATQ$, $SATQ$3d5eb413-328a-4e40-88e5-debcb6d91aad$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Lines, angles, and triangles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A line intersects two parallel lines, forming four acute angles and four obtuse angles. The measure of one of the acute angles is <math alttext="left parenthesis 9 x minus 560 right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>560</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of one of the acute angles and three of the obtuse angles is <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 18 x plus w right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the value of <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1660"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1660"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="1,660"><mn>1,660</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a line intersects two parallel lines, forming four acute angles and four obtuse angles. When two parallel lines are intersected by a transversal line, the angles formed have the following properties: two adjacent angles are supplementary, and alternate interior angles are congruent. Therefore, each of the four acute angles have the same measure, and each of the four obtuse angles have the same measure. It&rsquo;s also given that the measure of one of the acute angles is <math alttext="left parenthesis 9 x minus 560 right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>560</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. If two angles are supplementary, then the sum of their measures is <math alttext="180 degree"><mn>180</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. Therefore, the measure of the obtuse angle adjacent to any of the acute angles is <math alttext="left parenthesis 180 minus left parenthesis 9 x minus 560 right parenthesis right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>560</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>, or <math alttext="left parenthesis 180 minus 9 x plus 560 right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>560</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 740 right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>740</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the sum of the measures of one of the acute angles and three of the obtuse angles is <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 18 x plus w right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. It follows that <math alttext="left parenthesis 9 x minus 560 right parenthesis plus 3 left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 740 right parenthesis equals left parenthesis minus 18 x plus w right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>560</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>740</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="9 x minus 560 minus 27 x plus 2,220 equals minus 18 x plus w"><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>560</mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>27</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2,220</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></math>, or <math alttext="minus 18 x plus 1,660 equals minus 18 x plus w"><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1,660</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></math>. Adding <math alttext="18 x"><mrow>
<mn>18</mn>
<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> to both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="1,660 equals w"><mn>1,660</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></math>.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f67255ea","external_id":"3d5eb413-328a-4e40-88e5-debcb6d91aad","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"f26bdbc2-0264-4d25-a130-056b7c39dba0","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A line intersects two parallel lines, forming four acute angles and four obtuse angles. The measure of one of the acute angles is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 9 x minus 560 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>560</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of one of the acute angles and three of the obtuse angles is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 18 x plus w right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["1660"],"correct_answer":["1660"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"1,660\"><mn>1,660</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a line intersects two parallel lines, forming four acute angles and four obtuse angles. When two parallel lines are intersected by a transversal line, the angles formed have the following properties: two adjacent angles are supplementary, and alternate interior angles are congruent. Therefore, each of the four acute angles have the same measure, and each of the four obtuse angles have the same measure. It&rsquo;s also given that the measure of one of the