i>\n\t<mi>N</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","externalid":"761b928d-225b-4b73-968f-a9b367e5083e","templateid":"617736a3-961b-44c8-b65b-54cf7e97e63e","vaultid":"0ae1a5fe-7408-4d7c-976f-522204c5d50b","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"9a07fbaf-d887-48d3-b66a-39761a0f4d4c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"upper M upper N equals 7\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>M</mi>\n\t\t<mi>N</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper S upper T equals 7\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t\t<mi>T</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4d1413f3-acee-4839-a540-6780521f9fc1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"upper M upper N equals 7\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>M</mi>\n\t\t<mi>N</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper S upper T equals 21\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t\t<mi>T</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>21</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d2be79b1-8021-465c-be8c-efd380d2f055","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The measures of angles <math alttext=\"upper M\"><mi>M</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"70 degree\"><mn>70</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"60 degree\"><mn>60</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math>, respectively.</p>"},{"id":"c7ff9c70-8979-4120-a820-359255e666e9","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The measures of angles <math alttext=\"upper M\"><mi>M</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"70 degree\"><mn>70</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math alttext=\"50 degree\"><mn>50</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math>, respectively.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1691007959838,"updateDate":1691007959838}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959838, 1691007959838),
    ($SATQ$f7e626b2$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$038033-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The dimensions of a right rectangular prism are 4&nbsp;inches by 5&nbsp;inches by 6&nbsp;inches. What is the surface area, in square inches, of the prism?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">30</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">74</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">120</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">148</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The surface area is found by summing the area of each face. A right rectangular prism consists of three pairs of congruent rectangles, so the surface area is found by multiplying the areas of three adjacent rectangles by 2 and adding these products. For this prism, the surface area is equal to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f7e626b2/img_000_1c1b1f0c.png" alt="2 times, open parenthesis, 4 times 5, close parenthesis, plus, 2 times, open parenthesis, 5 times 6, close parenthesis, plus, 2 times, open parenthesis, 4 times 6, close parenthesis"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f7e626b2/img_001_8b83dba6.png" alt="2 times 20, plus, 2 times 30, plus, 2 times 24"></span>, which is equal to 148.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the area of one of the faces of the prism. Choice B is incorrect and may result from adding the areas of three adjacent rectangles without multiplying by 2. Choice C is incorrect. This is the volume, in cubic inches, of the prism.</p></p>
