$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["97"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 97. The intersecting lines form a triangle, and the angle with measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_001_2e99d9a6.png" alt="x degrees"></span> is an exterior angle of this triangle. The measure of an exterior angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two nonadjacent interior angles of the triangle. One of these angles has measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_002_d65b0dd4.png" alt="23 degrees"></span> and the other, which is supplementary to the angle with measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_003_962702a2.png" alt="106 degrees"></span>, has measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_004_715492b1.png" alt="180 degrees minus 106 degrees, equals 74 degrees"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class="italic">x</span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_005_af97dabc.png" alt="23 plus 74, equals 97"></span>.</p>
$SATQ$, true, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"f88f27e5","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"05759-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\">\n\t<div class=\"passage \">\n\t\t<div class=\"prose style:1 \">\n\t\t\t<p class=\"passage_para \">Intersecting lines <span class=\"italic\">r</span>, <span class=\"italic\">s</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">t</span> are shown below.</p>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n\n\t<div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_000_8689b68a.png\" alt=\"The figure presents three intersecting lines, labeled r, s, and t. Line s begins near the top of the figure and extends downward and slightly to the left. Line t begins to the left of line s, and extends downward and to the right, intersecting line s. Line r begins below line t and to the left of line s. Line r extends upward and to the right, first intersecting line s and then line t. The following angle measures are indicated: the angle formed to the right of line s and above line t measures 106 degrees, and the angle formed to the left of line s and above line r measures x degrees. The angle formed below line t and above line r measures 23 degrees.\" width=\"155\" height=\"87\"></div>\n</div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">What is the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["97"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 97. The intersecting lines form a triangle, and the angle with measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_001_2e99d9a6.png\" alt=\"x degrees\"></span> is an exterior angle of this triangle. The measure of an exterior angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two nonadjacent interior angles of the triangle. One of these angles has measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_002_d65b0dd4.png\" alt=\"23 degrees\"></span> and the other, which is supplementary to the angle with measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_003_962702a2.png\" alt=\"106 degrees\"></span>, has measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_004_715492b1.png\" alt=\"180 degrees minus 106 degrees, equals 74 degrees\"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/f88f27e5/img_005_af97dabc.png\" alt=\"23 plus 74, equals 97\"></span>.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":6,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959630,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"f88f27e5","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959630,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"05759-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"04ea6ab1-f8ca-4ba1-bc73-70d31103499d","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"05759-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\">\n\t<div class=\"passage \">\n\t\t<div class=\"prose style:1 \">\n\t\t\t<p class=\"passage_para \">Intersecting lines <span class=\"italic\">r</span>, <span class=\"italic\">s</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">t</span> are shown below.</p>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n\n\t<div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents three intersecting lines, labeled r, s, and t. Line s begins near the top of the figure and extends downward and slightly to the left. Line t begins to the left of line s, and extends downward and to the right, intersecting line s. Line r begins below line t and to the left of line s. Line r extends upward and to the right, first intersecting line s and then line t. The following angle measures are indicated: the angle formed to the right of line s and above line t measures 106 degrees, and the angle formed to the left of line s and above line r measures x degrees. The angle formed below line t and above line r measures 23 degrees.\" width=\"155\" height=\"87\"></div>\n</div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">What is the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 97. The intersecting lines form a triangle, and the angle with measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x degrees\"></span> is an exterior angle of this triangle. The measure of an exterior angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two nonadjacent interior angles of the triangle. One of these angles has measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"23 degrees\"></span> and the other, which is supplementary to the angle with measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"106 degrees\"></span>, has measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees minus 106 degrees, equals 74 degrees\"></span>. Therefore, the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"23 plus 74, equals 97\"></span>.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959630,"updateDate":1691007959630,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959630, 1691007959630),
    ($SATQ$f9d40000$SATQ$, $SATQ$b3738b72-9c5a-45b5-986b-00bb9643ab90$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$c1a4a3cb-8de7-4e9c-b91c-2a7fc6e7da44$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Lines, angles, and triangles$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>In <math alttext="triangle upper X upper Y upper Z"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></math>, the measure of <math alttext="angle upper X"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>X</mi></math><em> </em>is <math alttext="23 degree"><mn>23</mn>
