</math>-plane, circle B is obtained by translating circle A to the right <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> units. Which equation represents circle B?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"dbb0bf18-6a75-48ad-84ed-168f975b4c72","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 7 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"93ba99fb-ab2a-4eec-ba38-585afa3c68a4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2515242e-abe9-483d-87ca-d4a982b59d87","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dcc1b700-6508-41ab-8326-f101bc6c0e7a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 1 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2515242e-abe9-483d-87ca-d4a982b59d87"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> units. It’s given that circle A has the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, which can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus left parenthesis negative 3 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals 1 squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h equals 7"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k equals negative 3"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r equals 1"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the center of circle A is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 7 comma negative 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and its radius is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> unit. If circle A is translated <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> units to the right, the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the center will increase by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math>, while the <em>y</em>-coordinate and the radius of the circle will remain unchanged. Translating the center of circle A to the right <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> units yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 7 plus 4 comma negative 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 11 comma negative 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the center of circle B is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 11 comma negative 3 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="11"><mn>11</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 3"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> into the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus left parenthesis negative 3 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals 1"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> represents circle B.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A down, rather than right, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A left, rather than right, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A up, rather than right, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"fa2771d5","external_id":"87f88638-07ba-4370-ae6b-d743f0fba4ad","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"6595fdb5-ff86-49e7-ac92-2f8de197064e","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Circle A has equation <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. In the <math alttext=\"x y\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>-plane, circle B is obtained by translating circle A to the right <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> units. Which equation represents circle B?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"dbb0bf18-6a75-48ad-84ed-168f975b4c72","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 7 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"93ba99fb-ab2a-4eec-ba38-585afa3c68a4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2515242e-abe9-483d-87ca-d4a982b59d87","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dcc1b700-6508-41ab-8326-f101bc6c0e7a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 1 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["2515242e-abe9-483d-87ca-d4a982b59d87"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> units. It’s given that circle A has the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, which can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus left parenthesis negative 3 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals 1 squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals 7\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals negative 3\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals 1\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the center of circle A is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and its radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> unit. If circle A is translated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units to the right, the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the center will increase by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>, while the <em>y</em>-coordinate and the radius of the circle will remain unchanged. Translating the center of circle A to the right <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 plus 4 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 11 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the center of circle B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 11 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 3\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> into the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus left parenthesis negative 3 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> represents circle B.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A down, rather than right, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A left, rather than right, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A up, rather than right, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017720,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"fa2771d5","skill_cd":"S.D.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Circles","createDate":1755117017720,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"87f88638-07ba-4370-ae6b-d743f0fba4ad","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"6595fdb5-ff86-49e7-ac92-2f8de197064e","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Circle A has equation <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. In the <math alttext=\"x y\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>-plane, circle B is obtained by translating circle A to the right <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> units. Which equation represents circle B?</p>","keys":["2515242e-abe9-483d-87ca-d4a982b59d87"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"dbb0bf18-6a75-48ad-84ed-168f975b4c72","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 7 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"93ba99fb-ab2a-4eec-ba38-585afa3c68a4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2515242e-abe9-483d-87ca-d4a982b59d87","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dcc1b700-6508-41ab-8326-f101bc6c0e7a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 1 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> units. It’s given that circle A has the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, which can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus left parenthesis negative 3 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals 1 squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals 7\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals negative 3\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals 1\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the center of circle A is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and its radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> unit. If circle A is translated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units to the right, the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the center will increase by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>, while the <em>y</em>-coordinate and the radius of the circle will remain unchanged. Translating the center of circle A to the right <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 plus 4 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 11 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the center of circle B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 11 comma negative 3 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 3\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> into the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus left parenthesis negative 3 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 11 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 1\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> represents circle B.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A down, rather than right, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A left, rather than right, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a circle obtained by shifting circle A up, rather than right, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> units.</p>","externalid":"87f88638-07ba-4370-ae6b-d743f0fba4ad","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1755117017720,"updateDate":1755117017720}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017720, 1755117017720),
    ($SATQ$fb58c0db$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$070632-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Points <span class="italic"><span class="italic ">A</span></span> and <span class="italic"><span class="italic ">B</span></span> lie on a circle with radius 1, and arc <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_000_2f3bb937.png" alt="A, B"></span></span> has length <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_001_a32ec6ef.png" alt="pi over 3"></span></span>. What fraction of the circumference of the circle is the length of arc <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_002_2f3bb937.png" alt="A, B"></span></span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["1/6",".1666",".1667","0.166","0.167"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_003_a06ac9c9.png" alt="one sixth"></span>. The circumference, <span class="italic">C</span>, of a circle is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_004_ccae4ab8.png" alt="C equals, 2 pi, r"></span>, where <span class="italic">r</span> is the length of the radius of the circle. For the given circle with a radius of 1, the circumference is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_005_412e8d79.png" alt="C equals, 2 pi, times 1"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_006_ecaf7648.png" alt="C equals, 2 pi"></span>. To find what fraction of the circumference the length of arc <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_007_2f3bb937.png" alt="A, B"></span> is, divide the length of the arc by the circumference, which gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_008_59bd5c55.png" alt="the fraction pi over 3, end fraction, divided by 2 pi"></span>. This division can be represented by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fb58c0db/img_009_64240fcb.png" alt="the fraction pi over 3, end fraction, times the fraction 1 over 2 pi, end fraction, equals one sixth"></span>. Note that 1/6, .1666, .1667, 0.166, and 0.167 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
