b","skill_cd":"S.D.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Circles","createDate":1691007959632,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"070632-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"c21801ca-b8b0-4c44-a207-2f0b75275ac5","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"070632-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Points <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">A</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">B</span></span> lie on a circle with radius 1, and arc <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, B\"></span></span> has length <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"pi over 3\"></span></span>. What fraction of the circumference of the circle is the length of arc <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, B\"></span></span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one sixth\"></span>. The circumference, <span class=\"italic\">C</span>, of a circle is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"C equals, 2 pi, r\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">r</span> is the length of the radius of the circle. For the given circle with a radius of 1, the circumference is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"C equals, 2 pi, times 1\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"C equals, 2 pi\"></span>. To find what fraction of the circumference the length of arc <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A, B\"></span> is, divide the length of the arc by the circumference, which gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction pi over 3, end fraction, divided by 2 pi\"></span>. This division can be represented by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction pi over 3, end fraction, times the fraction 1 over 2 pi, end fraction, equals one sixth\"></span>. Note that 1/6, .1666, .1667, 0.166, and 0.167 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959632,"updateDate":1691007959632,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959632, 1691007959632),
