quation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n equals 18\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>. Therefore, the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the solution to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"three oneths equals StartFraction 6 Over n EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one third equals StartFraction 6 Over n EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the length of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper T upper U\"><mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the length of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper T upper U\"><mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> and the perimeter of triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper T upper U upper V\"><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi></math>, not the length of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&